winemac, win32u: a menu switch for MetalFX upscaling, and a render size

View > MetalFX Upscaling (Control-Command-U) switches, while the program runs, whether a
picture smaller than its window is upscaled by MetalFX. It sets the state of the notification
"finewine.metalfx.<process id>", which DXMT and MoltenVK look at (patches/dxmt/0007,
patches/moltenvk/0006).

FINEWINE_RENDER_SCALE=<percent, 25 to 99> makes programs see a screen that many percent of the
real one in each direction. It turns Wine's display mode emulation on (EmulateModeset) and
makes the mode a program finds when it starts an emulated one of that size, as if it had been
chosen in a game's settings. A game then draws that many pixels and MetalFX brings the picture
to the real size; everything else is scaled by Wine. The mode is given once per size (kept as
FineWineRenderScale beside the modes), so a program's own later choice stays.

Wine keeps the relation between an emulated mode and the real one as a fraction of two 16-bit
numbers multiplied by the DPI, and stops with an assertion for sizes that do not reduce that
far (3024x1964 at 75% rounded to 2268x1474 did). The nearest size that does, for every DPI a
prefix can have, is taken, an even one where possible.

